  "IMPLEMENTED": [
    "The existing original registry entry retains its captured closer and its actual call phase. No replacement HANDLE owner, serialized phase flag or new generic registry framework.",
    "PRE_SDK: only the original owner may recheck all original ancillary/child terminal facts and original Job emptiness before one native close.",
    "NATIVE_UNKNOWN: set before the captured CloseHandle invocation; exceptions, FALSE/malformed returns and normalization failures remain sticky. No later Job query, native close, closer substitution or replacement Job.",
    "NATIVE_CONFIRMED: recorded only after exact BOOL normalization succeeds. Local registry/binding/factory completion may recover from before/after-mutation bookkeeping errors without SDK reentry.",
    "Original factory close borrows the exact captured call. A new public cleanup request can finish a proven pre-SDK deferral; cached UNKNOWN replay remains unchanged and has no effects.",
    "Original first cause and source/registry/closer identities remain; private API/factory references retain confirmed results across binding-pop and terminal acknowledgement failures."
  ],
